{"body":"## Context\n\nIndependent review of #1185 found a pre-existing race at the public `AuthInterceptor.refreshToken` callback boundary. Root reproduced it on both original main `fce3f2812c8` and PR #1195 head `869a5cc1e2e`. It requires a custom callback that delays returning after the repository has finished; stock provider wiring returns the repository future directly.\n\n1. A 401 calls a wrapper around `repository.refreshToken()`. The repository rotates R1 to R2 and persists access-R2. Hold the wrapper before it returns that result to the interceptor.\n2. A manual repository refresh legitimately rotates R2 to R3 and persists access-R3 / R3.\n3. Release the wrapper. `AuthInterceptor._handle401Error` unconditionally writes its older `access-R2` and replays with it, leaving a mismatched credential set.\n\nBoth baseline and current reproduction report:\n\n```\nboundary before interceptor returns: access-R3; finalaccess=access-R2; finalrefresh=R3; servervalid=R3\nExpected: access-R3\nActual: access-R2\n```\n\n`SecureTokenStore` write ordering cannot prevent this: the stale write is issued after the newer one. This is separate from sharing a still-running repository rotation in #1185. A public custom refresher may await tracing or other work after a repository call; its result must not overwrite newer credentials in the same session.\n\nReproduction artifacts are retained with the #1185 review on the evidence branch: [current log](https://github.com/koniz-dev/flutter-starter/blob/evidence/docs/verification/issue-1185/boundary-current.log), [baseline log](https://github.com/koniz-dev/flutter-starter/blob/evidence/docs/verification/issue-1185/boundary-baseline.log), [probe source](https://github.com/koniz-dev/flutter-starter/blob/evidence/docs/verification/issue-1185/boundary-test.dart).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A tier-1 test holds the callback after a successful repository refresh, finishes a later repository refresh in the same session, then releases the callback. The interceptor must not overwrite the newer access token or replay with the superseded token. The test fails before the fix.\n- A custom refresher that returns a new token without persisting it still works: the interceptor stores it and replays successfully.\n- Existing session-generation, logout, queued replay and refresh failure tests remain green.\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOQVGyw88AAAABlD81Gw","author":{"login":"koniz-dev"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"The first network-only read/compare/write prototype is insufficient: root and independent review reproduced stale access reads that finish after a newer rotation, including the real SecureTokenStore timeout-bypass path. No prototype code was merged.\n\nSplit the required versioned-snapshot/conditional-adoption primitive into #1206 (`epic:core-storage`), including custom-store migration and storage ordering/repair tests. This issue retains network adoption/replay and its original acceptance criteria. Resume after #1206 closes; then use the new primitive and rerun delayed-callback, custom nonpersisting callback, session-generation and queue cases. The session is continuing the prerequisite serially.\n","createdAt":"2026-11-10T23:26:31Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/koniz-dev/flutter-starter/issues/1196#issuecomment-6782137627","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOQVGyw88AAAABlEo46Q","author":{"login":"koniz-dev"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Storage prerequisite #1206 is closed with merged PR #1207, committed evidence and custom-store migration notes. Resuming the network adoption/replay work from the merged versioned contract; the archived read/compare/write prototype remains unmerged.","createdAt":"2026-11-11T00:07:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/koniz-dev/flutter-starter/issues/1196#issuecomment-6782859497","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"title":"fix(network): delayed refresh callbacks overwrite newer access tokens"}

